1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:04,429
[Woman On P.A.]
Dr. Lee, call 4142.

2
00:00:04,507 --> 00:00:07,105
Dr. Lee, 4142.

3
00:00:16,206 --> 00:00:18,143
Will it, uh, be much longer?

4
00:00:18,212 --> 00:00:20,149
We'll call you when we're ready.

5
00:00:20,217 --> 00:00:22,154
I've been waiting
almost an hour.

6
00:00:22,223 --> 00:00:24,661
We'll call you when we're ready.

7
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:26,667
I'm sorry.

8
00:00:38,937 --> 00:00:40,874
[Man]
Saw him make quite a throw yesterday.

9
00:00:40,942 --> 00:00:43,642
There's a liner to left field
coming to third base's right.

10
00:00:43,716 --> 00:00:47,158
Laskowski is up.
The throw on the way to the plate.

11
00:00:47,225 --> 00:00:49,493
So she's really coming back?

12
00:00:49,566 --> 00:00:51,503
Who's coming back?

13
00:00:51,571 --> 00:00:53,542
You don't know her.

14
00:00:53,610 --> 00:00:57,849
You give her a raise?
Increase her benefits?

15
00:00:57,923 --> 00:01:01,365
Don't have TiVo on this thing.
Can't rewind. Shut up.

16
00:01:02,602 --> 00:01:06,670
You lower her hours?
You don't even know her.

17
00:01:06,747 --> 00:01:10,051
Who is this guy?
He's a patient.

18
00:01:10,123 --> 00:01:14,123
He's examining me.
He's gotta go back to work as soon
as I'm done with the examination.

19
00:01:15,638 --> 00:01:17,575
Guess I do too.

20
00:01:17,644 --> 00:01:21,245
It's gotta be something.
I mean, she didn't come back
because she likes you.

21
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:23,257
Mmm.

22
00:01:24,831 --> 00:01:27,463
Wait a minute.

23
00:01:27,538 --> 00:01:29,908
She did come back
because she likes you.

24
00:01:29,978 --> 00:01:33,511
[Giggling]
You dog. You slept with her.

25
00:01:33,588 --> 00:01:36,858
Keep talking.
I'll finish your exam
with a prostate check.

26
00:01:38,569 --> 00:01:40,506
I've agreed to take her
on one date.

27
00:01:40,575 --> 00:01:43,481
- What?
- So, you into this girl?

28
00:01:43,549 --> 00:01:46,956
- Yes.
- No. She- She's not giving me any choice.

29
00:01:47,025 --> 00:01:50,694
Wait. She's making you do her?

30
00:01:50,769 --> 00:01:52,706
Date her.

31
00:01:52,775 --> 00:01:57,048
Young ingenue doctor falling in love
with gruff, older mentor-

32
00:01:57,120 --> 00:02:00,823
Her sweet, gentle nature
bringing him to a closer,

33
00:02:00,898 --> 00:02:03,393
fuller understanding
of his wounded heart.

34
00:02:03,472 --> 00:02:05,135
Do her...

35
00:02:06,313 --> 00:02:08,546
or you're gay.

36
00:02:08,619 --> 00:02:11,285
For God's sakes.

37
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:15,531
[Together]
~ Sitting in a tree, K-l-S-S-l-N-G ~
Grow up. And learn to harmonize.

38
00:02:16,608 --> 00:02:19,046
- Oh!
- Damn it!

39
00:02:19,115 --> 00:02:23,115
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
- Who the hell walks around
with an open urine sample?

40
00:02:23,193 --> 00:02:26,224
I'm sorry. I didn't- I didn't-

41
00:02:27,271 --> 00:02:29,242
Uh-

42
00:02:32,953 --> 00:02:34,890
You think that was a bit
of an overreaction?

43
00:02:34,959 --> 00:02:38,492
Well, he peed on me.
I'm not into that.

44
00:02:38,569 --> 00:02:40,506
It's apple juice.

45
00:02:40,575 --> 00:02:42,512
Now go find that guy
and apologize.

46
00:02:42,581 --> 00:02:46,216
One more patient complaint
and you're looking at a suspension.

47
00:02:47,928 --> 00:02:49,865
[Sighs]

48
00:02:49,934 --> 00:02:52,236
[Panting]

49
00:02:56,787 --> 00:03:00,091
I forgive you for ruining my jacket.

50
00:03:01,232 --> 00:03:05,004
Look, you seem like
a regular kind of guy-

51
00:03:05,077 --> 00:03:07,105
not the type to get
another regular guy into trouble.

52
00:03:07,182 --> 00:03:09,119
Am I right?

53
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:11,250
[Sobbing]
[Sighs]

54
00:03:11,327 --> 00:03:16,399
- Twenty bucks cash if you'll stop crying.
- [Continues Sobbing]

55
00:03:16,475 --> 00:03:20,110
Forgive me. Yell at me.
Just give me something I can work with, okay?

56
00:03:20,185 --> 00:03:23,159
[Gagging]

57
00:03:34,091 --> 00:03:36,028
[Wilson]
Game's over.

58
00:03:36,096 --> 00:03:38,432
You two make nice?
Get a wheelchair.

59
00:03:38,502 --> 00:03:40,974
Get this guy into the E.R.
What happened?

60
00:03:41,043 --> 00:03:43,641
- Right pupil's blown.
- Holy-

61
00:03:43,717 --> 00:03:46,281
You gave the guy a stroke?

62
00:03:46,357 --> 00:03:48,469
[Groaning]

63
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:25,464
So the bear wipes himself
with the rabbit.

64
00:04:26,876 --> 00:04:28,902
Lame.

65
00:04:29,985 --> 00:04:32,319
Hey.
Yo.

66
00:04:32,389 --> 00:04:34,655
What are you doing here?
I work here.

67
00:04:34,728 --> 00:04:37,164
"Here" here? In this office?

68
00:04:37,233 --> 00:04:39,429
House practically begged me
to come back.

69
00:04:39,505 --> 00:04:41,998
- Please tell me you took him to the cleaners.
- Same lousy salary.

70
00:04:42,076 --> 00:04:47,108
- Then why'd you do it?
- Because this is the happiest place on Earth.

71
00:04:47,188 --> 00:04:50,523
Twenty-one-year-old male-
Comes in with grinding of the teeth.

72
00:04:50,596 --> 00:04:54,365
And House gives him a stroke.
Totally blew out his pupil.

73
00:04:54,437 --> 00:04:57,898
- You scared a guy into stroking out?
- Does that surprise anyone here?

74
00:04:57,978 --> 00:05:01,382
Blown pupils usually means
brain stem edema.
Sure,

75
00:05:01,452 --> 00:05:04,947
but since he's not dead or in a coma,
I'm going with stroke to the optic nerve.

76
00:05:05,026 --> 00:05:08,226
C.T. Scan shows two things.

77
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:10,496
Ischemia- death of brain tissue.

78
00:05:10,571 --> 00:05:12,767
Means there's been some damage,
hopefully not permanent.

79
00:05:12,843 --> 00:05:18,150
- And?
- And that's it. There's nothing there
to tell us what the underlying cause is.

80
00:05:18,222 --> 00:05:21,956
- Gotta do an M.R.I.
- You're looking at the wrong part
of the scan.

81
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:25,434
- I'm looking at the brain.
What else is there?
- The jaw.

82
00:05:25,504 --> 00:05:27,997
The jaw tells us why he stroked?

83
00:05:28,077 --> 00:05:31,049
No, the jaw tells us
why we can't do an M.R.I.

84
00:05:31,117 --> 00:05:33,713
Unless we want his jawbone
flying across the room.

85
00:05:33,789 --> 00:05:37,592
Metal plate. He's had major reconstruction,
and there's no way we're removing it,

86
00:05:37,664 --> 00:05:39,633
so we're forced to be clever.

87
00:05:39,701 --> 00:05:42,001
Angiogram to rule out vasculitis,

88
00:05:42,074 --> 00:05:46,014
E.M.G. For peripheral neuropathy,
tox screen to eliminate drugs,

89
00:05:46,083 --> 00:05:48,919
and echo to rule out cardiac emboli.

90
00:05:51,226 --> 00:05:56,692
Dr. Cameron, I'd appreciate you keeping
the terms of your new contract to yourself.

91
00:05:56,772 --> 00:05:59,869
Don't want everyone
clamoring for the same perks.

92
00:06:04,455 --> 00:06:06,891
What perks?
Nothing you'd be interested in.

93
00:06:06,961 --> 00:06:09,727
So it's not money, then?
Office space, insurance, parking-

94
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:12,236
Anything he could offer you,
we'd be interested in.

95
00:06:12,306 --> 00:06:15,403
He agreed to go
on a date with me.

96
00:06:15,478 --> 00:06:19,418
A date? Date, dinner and a movie,
naked and sweaty, date?

97
00:06:19,488 --> 00:06:22,084
He only committed to the first two.

98
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:24,460
He's so- He's so old.

99
00:06:24,533 --> 00:06:28,302
- And you're so young.
- It's a big mistake.

100
00:06:28,373 --> 00:06:30,935
It's my boss.
I'm allowed to sexually harass my boss.

101
00:06:31,013 --> 00:06:34,110
I'll arrange for the E.M.G.
You want to set up the angiogram?

102
00:06:34,187 --> 00:06:37,250
And you can get the blood samples,
patient history, patient consent.

103
00:06:39,698 --> 00:06:41,633
[Laughs]

104
00:06:41,702 --> 00:06:44,606
Like watching an accident
about to happen.

105
00:06:50,923 --> 00:06:52,858
Morning.

106
00:06:54,530 --> 00:06:56,898
Harvey, I'm Dr. Foreman.
I'm here to discuss your case.

107
00:06:59,474 --> 00:07:01,409
I'm Annette.
I'm Harvey's friend.

108
00:07:01,479 --> 00:07:03,414
Nice to meet you.

109
00:07:03,483 --> 00:07:08,152
I need your next of kin.
You didn't fill that out on your intake form.

110
00:07:08,227 --> 00:07:10,025
Harvey's parents are dead.

111
00:07:10,098 --> 00:07:12,864
They died two years ago
in a car crash.

112
00:07:14,039 --> 00:07:16,840
I see.
So, Harvey, you have any siblings?

113
00:07:16,912 --> 00:07:19,610
No. And no grandparents,

114
00:07:19,685 --> 00:07:22,885
or uncles or aunts.

115
00:07:22,959 --> 00:07:25,954
Annette, uh, I don't want to have
to ask you to leave-

116
00:07:26,033 --> 00:07:28,503
I want her to stay.

117
00:07:28,571 --> 00:07:31,600
Well, she can stay.
You do the talking.

118
00:07:38,726 --> 00:07:41,424
Why'd you come to the clinic this morning?

119
00:07:41,499 --> 00:07:45,837
Uh, about six months ago,
I started grinding my-

120
00:07:49,016 --> 00:07:52,250
You know. In your mouth.
You chew with them.

121
00:07:53,893 --> 00:07:56,159
Teeth.

122
00:07:56,230 --> 00:07:59,327
Harvey's experiencing
a little nominal aphasia.
Hmm.

123
00:07:59,404 --> 00:08:01,339
You know, when you can't
remember nouns.

124
00:08:01,409 --> 00:08:03,435
Yeah, I think I know
what nominal aphasia is.

125
00:08:03,514 --> 00:08:05,506
Have you had any treatment
for the teeth grinding?

126
00:08:05,584 --> 00:08:07,986
I went to a-

127
00:08:08,057 --> 00:08:12,624
You know, they do that thing
with the sharp pointy things.

128
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:15,068
- Needles? Someone took your blood?
- No. They make you breathe.

129
00:08:15,139 --> 00:08:18,077
- Pulmonologist?
- No. She had this, uh-

130
00:08:18,146 --> 00:08:20,912
She had this electrical machine.

131
00:08:20,985 --> 00:08:22,920
He saw an acupuncturist.

132
00:08:22,989 --> 00:08:25,255
Mm-hmm.

133
00:08:27,933 --> 00:08:30,871
Do you know
what the acupuncturist did?

134
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:33,570
She diagnosed liver chi stagnation
and sent Harvey to a shen balancer.

135
00:08:33,645 --> 00:08:38,109
He referred him
to a homeopathic doctor,
who sent him to a chiropractor.

136
00:08:38,188 --> 00:08:42,926
Naturally.
The chiropractor thought it might be food
sensitivity and sent Harvey to a naturopath.

137
00:08:42,999 --> 00:08:45,731
The naturopath sent me
back to the-

138
00:08:45,805 --> 00:08:48,743
- Back to the acupuncturist.
- Yes.

139
00:08:48,811 --> 00:08:52,045
Okay. Well, we'll need to see
the records...

140
00:08:52,119 --> 00:08:55,057
of all of those, uh, practitioners.

141
00:08:55,126 --> 00:08:57,061
Okay.
Thank you.

142
00:09:02,141 --> 00:09:04,110
Everything set for the angiogram?

143
00:09:04,178 --> 00:09:07,513
Cameron's got the E.M.G. First.
Who's that?

144
00:09:07,586 --> 00:09:09,852
Harvey's guru.

145
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:14,331
- That's what she called herself?
- That's what she acted like.

146
00:09:27,563 --> 00:09:30,729
Hi. I'm having vaginal pain.

147
00:09:33,375 --> 00:09:35,310
Pleasure to meet you.

148
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:40,015
My OB/GYN died recently.
He was a nice man.

149
00:09:40,089 --> 00:09:44,325
- Warm hands.
- Not anymore.

150
00:09:44,399 --> 00:09:46,995
So, does it hurt when you tinkle?

151
00:09:47,072 --> 00:09:50,875
Yeah, that's when it's worst.

152
00:09:51,915 --> 00:09:54,887
You have some vaginal tearing.

153
00:09:54,955 --> 00:09:56,890
No sign of bruising.

154
00:09:56,959 --> 00:09:59,293
No indication of trauma,
forced entry.

155
00:10:00,834 --> 00:10:03,863
Ramona, you naughty girl.

156
00:10:03,941 --> 00:10:06,879
Either you've got yourself
an 18-year-old boyfriend,

157
00:10:06,947 --> 00:10:09,543
or an 80-year-old
with some little blue pills.

158
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:11,816
Myron thought he'd just try 'em out.

159
00:10:11,891 --> 00:10:15,557
- Lucky you.
- [Sighs] I guess.

160
00:10:15,633 --> 00:10:17,568
You'd prefer it if Myron was a little...

161
00:10:17,637 --> 00:10:20,335
droopier?
Maybe a little.

162
00:10:20,410 --> 00:10:24,578
We used to hold hands
or read together...

163
00:10:24,653 --> 00:10:26,747
or watch Jeopardy.

164
00:10:26,824 --> 00:10:31,128
I haven't seen Jeopardy
in almost a month.

165
00:10:32,504 --> 00:10:34,439
Have you talked to him about this?

166
00:10:34,507 --> 00:10:37,536
You try talking a 73-year-old
out of sex.

167
00:10:37,615 --> 00:10:41,817
With all these male enhancements,
the pressure to put out's incredible.

168
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:45,022
It's worse than high school.

169
00:10:45,097 --> 00:10:48,866
He doesn't get what he wants from me,
he'll get it from Connie
in the corner condo.

170
00:10:48,939 --> 00:10:53,812
She's dying her hair red.
Major league slut.

171
00:10:56,756 --> 00:10:58,987
[Clears Throat]
Here's a prescription...

172
00:10:59,060 --> 00:11:01,428
for vaginal estrogen suppositories.

173
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:04,027
It'll help with the lubrication.

174
00:11:04,104 --> 00:11:06,039
Thank you.

175
00:11:07,178 --> 00:11:09,671
Maybe you could give Myron
a prescription-

176
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:11,912
something weaker
than he's got now.

177
00:11:11,988 --> 00:11:15,757
Tell him it's better for his heart.
He'd buy that.

178
00:11:15,830 --> 00:11:18,768
You can't tell him the truth
so you want me to lie to him?

179
00:11:18,837 --> 00:11:22,777
- Would you?
- Close your legs.

180
00:11:24,048 --> 00:11:26,040
[Sighs]

181
00:11:27,556 --> 00:11:31,154
Nerves stimulate muscles to move
by creating a small electrical current.

182
00:11:31,230 --> 00:11:33,894
The machine will measure that.

183
00:11:34,971 --> 00:11:39,504
And I will insert this needle
into various muscles and ask you to flex.

184
00:11:39,582 --> 00:11:44,115
Sometimes it can be painful.
Let me know. I can pull back.

185
00:11:44,191 --> 00:11:45,989
No.

186
00:11:46,062 --> 00:11:48,362
I mean, it's okay.

187
00:11:49,369 --> 00:11:51,771
Okay. Put your arm out to the side.

188
00:11:57,921 --> 00:12:00,015
[Moans]

189
00:12:00,093 --> 00:12:03,657
- You all right?
- I'm good.

190
00:12:03,734 --> 00:12:05,726
You don't have to stop.

191
00:12:05,806 --> 00:12:07,832
[Monitor Beeping]

192
00:12:07,910 --> 00:12:09,845
Raise your arm over your head.

193
00:12:15,225 --> 00:12:17,821
[Moans]

194
00:12:17,898 --> 00:12:21,861
[Monitor Beeping]

195
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:23,875
[Cameron]
The E.M.G. Was clean.

196
00:12:23,945 --> 00:12:27,942
[House]
Based on this history,
it's either toxic herbs from the homeopath,

197
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:30,616
spinal damage
from the chiropractor,

198
00:12:30,693 --> 00:12:34,291
infection from a needle
that the acupuncturist
accidentally let sit in eye of newt,

199
00:12:34,367 --> 00:12:36,598
or the shen balancer-

200
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:39,973
What the hell is a shen,
and how come it's lopsided?

201
00:12:40,047 --> 00:12:42,779
The only abnormal test result
we found was on the echo report.

202
00:12:42,852 --> 00:12:45,014
Mitral valve prolapse.

203
00:12:45,091 --> 00:12:49,031
Hang up a shingle and condemn
the narrowness and greed
of Western medicine.

204
00:12:49,099 --> 00:12:51,091
You can make a damn fine living.

205
00:12:51,171 --> 00:12:54,974
Clots form on the faulty valve,
get sent to the brain,
voila- stroke.

206
00:12:55,046 --> 00:12:57,778
[House]
Of course, no harm, no foul.

207
00:12:57,852 --> 00:13:00,254
Just taking a few bucks
from superstitious idiots, right?

208
00:13:01,794 --> 00:13:04,162
Could also be an aneurysm
due to trauma.

209
00:13:04,232 --> 00:13:07,796
Trauma?
From what, the chiropractic treatments?

210
00:13:07,873 --> 00:13:11,710
It's bacterial endocarditis,
an infected valve.
We should do blood cultures.

211
00:13:11,781 --> 00:13:13,977
The six months that he had
with these charlatans...

212
00:13:14,054 --> 00:13:17,584
might have been better spent
going to someone who looks at things
that exist in the real world.

213
00:13:17,661 --> 00:13:20,131
But that's just me
being all narrow again.

214
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:23,104
I noticed a small bruit
when I listened to Harvey's
left carotid.

215
00:13:23,173 --> 00:13:25,267
You could hear that
if he had an aneurysm from trauma.

216
00:13:25,345 --> 00:13:27,337
An aneurysm would have shown
on the angiogram.

217
00:13:27,415 --> 00:13:29,977
No. Not necessarily.

218
00:13:30,991 --> 00:13:32,926
Hmm.

219
00:13:32,994 --> 00:13:35,020
Quite a dilemma.

220
00:13:35,099 --> 00:13:40,063
Oh, great pool-hall oracle,
grant me guidance.

221
00:13:40,143 --> 00:13:44,710
Do we go with Foreman's theory,
which is at least marginally supported
by medical test results,

222
00:13:44,786 --> 00:13:48,350
or Chase's theory,
that is completely unsupported
by medical evidence?

223
00:13:48,428 --> 00:13:50,420
What to do?

224
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:52,435
The guy obviously broke his jaw
somehow.

225
00:13:52,503 --> 00:13:55,475
Who knows what other trauma he's suffered?
We should do the angiogram again.

226
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:58,674
And all signs point to-

227
00:13:58,749 --> 00:14:02,780
Ah. Sorry, Chase.
The gods have spoken.

228
00:14:02,859 --> 00:14:06,389
Start Harvey on blood thinners
and antibiotics.

229
00:14:06,467 --> 00:14:09,633
Wow. Yeah, I get it.
House is adorable.

230
00:14:09,708 --> 00:14:12,646
I just want to hold him
and never let go.

231
00:14:15,219 --> 00:14:17,245
[Choking]

232
00:14:17,324 --> 00:14:21,093
- My God! What the hell are you doing?
- [Gasps]

233
00:14:21,165 --> 00:14:24,262
- She's choking him.
- Foreman, stop. Let her go.

234
00:14:24,339 --> 00:14:26,605
- She was trying to kill him.
- No. No, she wasn't.

235
00:14:26,677 --> 00:14:29,978
His vitals seem okay.
Please- Please, don't hurt her.

236
00:14:31,688 --> 00:14:33,954
What the hell is going on in here?

237
00:14:37,234 --> 00:14:39,670
