471
00:27:40,164 --> 00:27:45,436
- They're gonna show up at the morgue.
- Be sure and let me know
when Cuddy starts screaming.

472
00:27:50,019 --> 00:27:53,389
You lied to them!
He told us our son was dead.

473
00:27:53,459 --> 00:27:56,089
It's only a white lie.

474
00:27:56,165 --> 00:27:59,194
Technically, all I did was
call them a little early.

475
00:27:59,273 --> 00:28:01,469
Trust me.
He'll be dead real soon.

476
00:28:01,544 --> 00:28:04,879
Actually, I saved you
some rush hour traffic.

477
00:28:04,951 --> 00:28:07,045
I'm calling our lawyer.

478
00:28:07,123 --> 00:28:11,063
Fine. Just as soon as you've signed
the surgery consent.

479
00:28:12,201 --> 00:28:14,432
I have a pen.

480
00:28:14,505 --> 00:28:16,440
[Beeping]

481
00:28:18,347 --> 00:28:22,846
Marilyn Park for Mark Lerner.
Yes, I'll hold.

482
00:28:22,924 --> 00:28:27,491
Harvey's your son.
I'm sure you still care about him.

483
00:28:27,567 --> 00:28:31,006
He humiliated us.

484
00:28:31,075 --> 00:28:34,673
Everybody we know knows about his...
perversion.

485
00:28:34,749 --> 00:28:38,449
But you don't get off on embarrassment
the way your son does.

486
00:28:38,524 --> 00:28:40,493
My guess, maybe it skips a generation.

487
00:28:40,562 --> 00:28:42,862
How much money would it take
to compensate you-

488
00:28:42,934 --> 00:28:46,065
Yeah, you guys can haggle in a minute,
but here's the thing.

489
00:28:46,142 --> 00:28:50,173
Humiliation comes in all kinds
of packages.

490
00:28:50,250 --> 00:28:52,185
People finding out
that your son's a perv.

491
00:28:52,254 --> 00:28:55,693
That's pretty high up there.

492
00:28:55,762 --> 00:28:59,633
People finding out that you'd
rather let your son die...

493
00:28:59,703 --> 00:29:02,139
than sign a piece of paper-

494
00:29:02,209 --> 00:29:04,201
where's that rank?

495
00:29:04,280 --> 00:29:07,343
Trust me,
if I have to paste up a sign...

496
00:29:07,420 --> 00:29:11,086
in every nail salon
and dumpling shop in Pennsylvania,
I'll make sure they know.

497
00:29:21,451 --> 00:29:23,386
[Beeps]

498
00:29:27,731 --> 00:29:31,261
Your son will be in surgery
first thing in the morning.

499
00:29:34,312 --> 00:29:37,579
Dumplings.
That was a cheap shot.

500
00:29:44,300 --> 00:29:47,066
Hi. Are you, uh-

501
00:29:47,140 --> 00:29:49,075
Can we talk?

502
00:29:49,144 --> 00:29:52,981
Gee, I wonder what this
is gonna be about.

503
00:29:54,322 --> 00:29:56,918
I just want to make sure
no one gets hurt.

504
00:29:56,994 --> 00:30:00,261
I will be fine.
Everybody's acting like I'm going out
with Jack the Ripper.

505
00:30:00,335 --> 00:30:04,298
Oh. It's not-
It's not you I'm worried about.

506
00:30:07,851 --> 00:30:11,848
It's been a long time
since he opened up to someone,
and l-

507
00:30:11,927 --> 00:30:15,058
You better be absolutely sure
you want this,

508
00:30:15,134 --> 00:30:19,039
because if he opens up again
and gets hurt-

509
00:30:20,311 --> 00:30:22,246
I don't think there's gonna be
a next time.

510
00:30:23,719 --> 00:30:25,847
You're worried
I'm gonna break his heart?

511
00:30:38,084 --> 00:30:40,350
The wide side's too short.

512
00:30:40,422 --> 00:30:42,790
You're gonna look like Lou Costello.

513
00:30:45,868 --> 00:30:47,962
This is a mistake.

514
00:30:48,037 --> 00:30:51,498
I don't know how to have
casual conversation.

515
00:30:51,579 --> 00:30:54,415
You think you're talking
about one thing,

516
00:30:54,485 --> 00:30:56,477
and either you are,
and it's incredibly boring,

517
00:30:56,557 --> 00:31:00,691
or you're not because there's a subtext,
and you need a decoder ring.

518
00:31:00,766 --> 00:31:03,362
Open doors for her.
Help her with her chair.

519
00:31:03,439 --> 00:31:07,709
- I have been on a date.
- Not since disco died.

520
00:31:07,781 --> 00:31:10,183
Comment on her shoes,
her earrings,

521
00:31:10,253 --> 00:31:13,282
and then move on
to D.H.A.

522
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:16,958
Her dreams, hopes and aspirations.

523
00:31:17,034 --> 00:31:19,835
Trust me. Panty peeler.

524
00:31:21,779 --> 00:31:24,876
- And if you need condoms, I've got some.
- Did your wife give them to you?

525
00:31:24,952 --> 00:31:29,359
Drug rep.
They've got antibiotics built in somehow.

526
00:31:29,428 --> 00:31:31,898
I should cancel.

527
00:31:31,967 --> 00:31:34,403
I've got a patient in surgery
tomorrow morning.

528
00:31:34,472 --> 00:31:37,410
And if you were a surgeon,
that would actually matter.

529
00:31:40,151 --> 00:31:43,123
That's a good idea.
Settle your nerves.
Get me a beer too.

530
00:31:43,191 --> 00:31:45,126
No beer.

531
00:31:45,196 --> 00:31:48,691
You're gonna eat before dinner?

532
00:31:56,787 --> 00:31:58,949
This is pretty lame, right?

533
00:32:02,465 --> 00:32:05,061
I think she likes lame.

534
00:32:06,408 --> 00:32:09,403
It's beautiful.

535
00:32:09,481 --> 00:32:11,416
And you look very handsome.

536
00:32:12,989 --> 00:32:14,924
Thank you.

537
00:32:14,994 --> 00:32:18,160
I've always loved this restaurant.

538
00:32:18,234 --> 00:32:22,675
Yeah. It's changed a lot
since the last time I was here.

539
00:32:22,744 --> 00:32:24,679
Used to be a strip joint.

540
00:32:24,748 --> 00:32:27,116
[Laughs]

541
00:32:29,358 --> 00:32:31,350
Nice earrings.

542
00:32:31,429 --> 00:32:34,161
My mom's. Thank you.

543
00:32:35,538 --> 00:32:37,666
Nice shoes.

544
00:32:37,743 --> 00:32:40,977
Comfortable?

545
00:32:41,050 --> 00:32:43,714
I'm not expecting you to be
someone you're not.

546
00:32:45,459 --> 00:32:47,394
We're in a restaurant.

547
00:32:47,464 --> 00:32:49,730
We're dressed up.
We're eating.

548
00:32:49,802 --> 00:32:52,706
Without small talk, what is there?

549
00:33:05,703 --> 00:33:07,638
[Sighs]

550
00:33:07,708 --> 00:33:09,974
According to Freud-
and I'm paraphrasing-

551
00:33:10,046 --> 00:33:14,715
the instinct of love toward an object
demands a mastery to obtain it,

552
00:33:14,790 --> 00:33:18,490
and if a person feels
they can't control the object,
or feel threatened by it,

553
00:33:18,564 --> 00:33:20,830
they act negatively toward it.

554
00:33:20,903 --> 00:33:23,932
Like an eighth-grade boy
punching a girl.

555
00:33:24,009 --> 00:33:28,074
I treat you like garbage,
so I must really like you.

556
00:33:32,428 --> 00:33:35,457
Given your Freudian theory,
what does it mean
if I start being nice to you?

557
00:33:35,535 --> 00:33:38,371
That you're getting in touch
with your feelings.

558
00:33:38,441 --> 00:33:40,535
Mm-hmm.

559
00:33:40,613 --> 00:33:44,313
So there's absolutely nothing I can do
to make you think that I don't like you?

560
00:33:44,388 --> 00:33:46,984
[Laughs]
Sorry, no.

561
00:33:52,405 --> 00:33:55,377
I have one evening with you-
one chance-

562
00:33:55,444 --> 00:33:58,883
and I don't want to waste it
talking about what wines
you like...

563
00:33:58,953 --> 00:34:00,888
or what movies you hate.

564
00:34:04,096 --> 00:34:09,437
I want to know how you feel.

565
00:34:09,508 --> 00:34:11,774
About me.

566
00:34:18,127 --> 00:34:22,899
You live under the delusion
that you can fix everything
that isn't perfect.

567
00:34:22,972 --> 00:34:27,208
That's why you married a man
who was dying of cancer.

568
00:34:28,215 --> 00:34:31,745
You don't love, you need.

569
00:34:31,823 --> 00:34:34,259
And now that your husband is dead,

570
00:34:34,329 --> 00:34:37,233
you're looking for your new
charity case.

571
00:34:37,302 --> 00:34:40,569
That's why you're
going out with me.

572
00:34:40,643 --> 00:34:42,578
I'm twice your age.

573
00:34:42,648 --> 00:34:44,879
I'm not great-looking.

574
00:34:44,952 --> 00:34:47,582
I'm not charming.
I'm not even nice.

575
00:34:49,996 --> 00:34:53,799
What I am is what you need.

576
00:34:53,872 --> 00:34:55,841
I'm damaged.

577
00:35:00,152 --> 00:35:02,679
[Woman Laughing]

578
00:35:13,246 --> 00:35:15,272
[Woman]
Warm saline.

579
00:35:15,351 --> 00:35:17,617
[Man]
3.0 silk-
[Indistinct]

580
00:35:17,689 --> 00:35:19,681
I'll get the-
[Indistinct]

581
00:35:23,702 --> 00:35:26,298
Came in late.
Good time last night?

582
00:35:26,376 --> 00:35:29,405
How's the surgery going?
Harvey's doing fine so far.

583
00:35:29,482 --> 00:35:32,579
- How'd the night go?
- It was fine. How was your evening?

584
00:35:34,259 --> 00:35:37,993
She had the ravioli.
I had the puttanesca.

585
00:35:38,067 --> 00:35:40,537
Yes, I really want to know
about the quality of the food.

586
00:35:40,606 --> 00:35:44,603
Either something very good happened
or something very bad.
Which is it?

587
00:35:44,681 --> 00:35:47,379
Well, I did have a little
indigestion afterwards.

588
00:35:47,455 --> 00:35:49,424
Maybe it was the garlic bread.

589
00:35:49,491 --> 00:35:52,292
Or the wine.
Something made my eyes puffy.

590
00:35:52,365 --> 00:35:55,565
- Crying in your pillow can do that.
- It was the wine.

591
00:35:55,638 --> 00:35:58,576
We had a nice candid conversation.

592
00:35:58,646 --> 00:36:03,145
Nothing deep.
Mostly small talk.
I'm sure.

593
00:36:03,222 --> 00:36:06,820
Took your advice.
Complimented her shoes.
That's 15 minutes of chat right there.

594
00:36:06,896 --> 00:36:11,269
- No snide comments?
- I guess-when we talked about you guys.

595
00:36:14,746 --> 00:36:17,512
- Just answer one question.
- You two gonna do dinner again?

596
00:36:19,022 --> 00:36:20,957
I... don't think so.

597
00:36:21,027 --> 00:36:23,725
I... don't know.

598
00:36:23,800 --> 00:36:26,966
Hey, kids.
You were wrong.

599
00:36:27,039 --> 00:36:29,475
No aneurysm, no nothin'.
This guy's clean.

600
00:36:31,549 --> 00:36:34,042
Which means we've got no idea
what's causing the strokes.

601
00:36:34,122 --> 00:36:36,057
He's had two more post-op.

602
00:36:36,126 --> 00:36:38,061
We won't know the extent
of the damage...

603
00:36:38,130 --> 00:36:40,224
until he comes out of the coma-
if he comes out.

604
00:36:40,302 --> 00:36:43,172
Maybe we should go back
to the blood thinners.
Up the dosage.

605
00:36:43,241 --> 00:36:47,682
If it's not clots, a loading dose
of blood thinners is gonna make him
bleed out of his ears.

606
00:36:47,751 --> 00:36:49,686
Then he won't be able to hear.

607
00:36:49,756 --> 00:36:52,887
- [Knocking]
- Oy vey.

608
00:36:52,963 --> 00:36:56,800
- Nobody home. Leave a message.
- This is important.

609
00:36:56,872 --> 00:36:59,068
[Sighs]

610
00:36:59,143 --> 00:37:02,377
Chase, Cameron, get another
angiogram and echo.

611
00:37:02,450 --> 00:37:04,385
You better get a full body scan.

612
00:37:04,454 --> 00:37:07,358
If it is clots, it'd be good
to know where they are.

613
00:37:11,737 --> 00:37:13,672
Sorry about that.

614
00:37:13,741 --> 00:37:16,303
Guy dying.

615
00:37:16,380 --> 00:37:19,146
Those pills you gave Myron?
They're not working.

616
00:37:19,220 --> 00:37:22,249
Well, good to see you've got
the correct perspective on the thing.

617
00:37:22,326 --> 00:37:24,922
Well, the old ones, I mean,
made me feel like a tree, you know?

618
00:37:24,999 --> 00:37:26,934
Nice visual.

619
00:37:27,003 --> 00:37:29,599
But the new ones,
I might as well be eating candy.

620
00:37:29,675 --> 00:37:31,769
Candy wouldn't take away
your headaches.
What?

621
00:37:31,847 --> 00:37:34,819
You came to me and told me
you were having too much sex.

622
00:37:34,887 --> 00:37:37,688
I never did.
You too, sequoia.

623
00:37:37,760 --> 00:37:40,492
- Well, no, that's not true. L-
- I know everybody lies,

624
00:37:40,566 --> 00:37:43,867
but you'd think that after
a certain amount of time together,
you wouldn't be trying so hard.

625
00:37:47,614 --> 00:37:50,984
- Your rings don't match.
- Why would they?

626
00:37:51,055 --> 00:37:55,827
The style is one thing,
but one silver, one gold?
How long have you guys been married?

627
00:37:55,899 --> 00:37:59,234
Fifty-five years.
Forty-nine years.

628
00:37:59,306 --> 00:38:02,437
Damn it. You're having an affair.

629
00:38:02,513 --> 00:38:05,040
Did you really say
you wanted to have less sex?

630
00:38:05,120 --> 00:38:08,957
Well, less.
If I wanted none,
I'd stay home with Esther.

631
00:38:09,028 --> 00:38:10,894
I just need a little rest.

632
00:38:10,965 --> 00:38:14,369
You guys aren't the victims
of the little blue pills,
you're the problem.

633
00:38:14,439 --> 00:38:16,635
- I'm sorry.
- Me too.

634
00:38:16,710 --> 00:38:18,736
I should just have told you how I felt.

635
00:38:18,815 --> 00:38:21,719
Aw.

636
00:38:23,860 --> 00:38:26,764
Oh, welcome to hell.

637
00:38:26,832 --> 00:38:28,824
[Both Cooing]

638
00:38:37,990 --> 00:38:39,925
Uh, hey,
how about the pills?

639
00:38:39,995 --> 00:38:43,832
Looks like you guys are good to go
drug-free for a while.

640
00:38:44,839 --> 00:38:49,143
Dr. Chase, these breath mints
you've been popping since yesterday-

641
00:38:49,214 --> 00:38:51,376
are they a new fetish?

642
00:38:51,453 --> 00:38:55,119
I found them at Harvey's.
What? I just took two boxes.

643
00:38:55,195 --> 00:38:58,861
- The guy's got a whole drawer of them.
- And you didn't find that interesting?

644
00:38:58,936 --> 00:39:01,167
Well, there's lots of interesting stuff
in his place.

645
00:39:01,241 --> 00:39:03,472
The mints weren't high up
on the list.

646
00:39:03,545 --> 00:39:05,571
Wrong.

647
00:39:19,947 --> 00:39:22,007
Chase, get your nose in here.

648
00:39:22,086 --> 00:39:24,180
If you're trying to humiliate me,

649
00:39:24,258 --> 00:39:27,059
I told you-
Come on.
Put your face in his mouth.

650
00:39:29,636 --> 00:39:31,571
[Clears Throat]

651
00:39:33,176 --> 00:39:35,544
- Ugh!
- Rich, wouldn't you say?

652
00:39:35,615 --> 00:39:37,743
Mm. Smells like old vomit.

653
00:39:37,819 --> 00:39:40,950
Number one sign
of fulminating osteomyelitis.

654
00:39:41,027 --> 00:39:43,223
Infection of the jaw?

655
00:39:43,299 --> 00:39:46,760
Probably from the original break.
Never healed properly.

656
00:39:46,839 --> 00:39:48,933
Infected tissue from the jaw...

657
00:39:49,010 --> 00:39:53,577
breaks off,
blocks blood flow to the brain.

658
00:39:53,655 --> 00:39:56,353
And life just isn't worth living
without blood.

659
00:39:56,428 --> 00:39:58,864
It was hidden from the scans
by the metal plate.

660
00:39:58,932 --> 00:40:02,530
And an infection in the jaw
is unlikely to show up in blood tests.

661
00:40:02,608 --> 00:40:05,170
- So how do we confirm?
- Like this.

662
00:40:18,241 --> 00:40:21,702
Ladies and gentlemen, we have pus.

663
00:40:24,054 --> 00:40:26,524
We're gonna remove the jaw.

664
00:40:27,328 --> 00:40:29,821
Anybody got a buzz saw?
Okay, call a surgeon.

665
00:40:32,439 --> 00:40:34,670
[Mechanical Whirring]

666
00:40:46,736 --> 00:40:49,229
[Indistinct Conversation]

667
00:41:01,435 --> 00:41:03,370
Hi. I'm Dr. House.

668
00:41:06,078 --> 00:41:08,013
How's tricks, Annette?

669
00:41:12,559 --> 00:41:14,494
I just wanted to see if he was okay.

670
00:41:14,563 --> 00:41:16,794
I'll leave.

671
00:41:16,868 --> 00:41:20,568
It's okay.
I came to talk to you both.

672
00:41:20,643 --> 00:41:22,805
Like I tell all my patients,

673
00:41:22,881 --> 00:41:25,647
you've simply got to say no
to strangulation.

674
00:41:27,692 --> 00:41:29,888
Me, I'm a freak.

675
00:41:29,963 --> 00:41:31,932
I get off on not being in pain.

676
00:41:32,001 --> 00:41:34,905
That and chocolate-covered
marshmallow bunnies.

677
00:41:34,974 --> 00:41:36,966
He's not a freak.

678
00:41:37,045 --> 00:41:39,572
Yeah, he is... a little.

679
00:41:39,651 --> 00:41:42,521
But it's gotta stop,

680
00:41:42,590 --> 00:41:44,821
or he'll die.

681
00:41:46,465 --> 00:41:49,403
It's not about pain.

682
00:41:49,472 --> 00:41:52,068
It's about being open.

683
00:41:52,144 --> 00:41:56,380
And completely vulnerable
to another person.

684
00:41:58,158 --> 00:42:01,756
If you can learn
to be that deeply trusting,

685
00:42:03,502 --> 00:42:05,733
it changes you.

686
00:42:13,691 --> 00:42:15,957
Lock him in a cage.

687
00:42:16,030 --> 00:42:18,261
That should be fine, medically.

688
00:42:21,708 --> 00:42:23,643
Dr. House?

689
00:42:27,054 --> 00:42:28,989
Were my parents here?

690
00:42:32,500 --> 00:42:34,800
Did they come to see me?

691
00:42:48,032 --> 00:42:51,766
~~ [Background]

692
00:43:13,053 --> 00:43:16,048
~ [Continues]

693
00:43:30,023 --> 00:43:32,151
~ [Ends]

694
00:44:06,436 --> 00:44:07,699
That's some bad hat, Harry.

